A '''video store''' was, presumably, a business that rented [[holodrama]]s. They were common on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]], where a [[Video Store|series of billboards]] were put up in order to advertise them, and attract potential customers.<ref name="DoM" /> One video store was located at the [[corner of twelfth and G]] on [[Level 1312]], next to [[Coruscant Underworld hotel|a hotel building]], although the sign was upside-down,<ref name="Catch">{{TCW|To Catch a Jedi}}</ref> and another sign was lying dumped on the ground nearby.<ref name="Wrong">{{TCW|The Wrong Jedi}}</ref> Another video store was located on [[Level 1313]], although once again, the sign was upside-down. Yet another video store was located at [[the wharf]], where several signs were put up on a building lying next to a lake.<ref name="Gone">{{TCW|Gone with a Trace}}</ref>

Video stores were also present in the [[central marketplace]] of [[Ro Station]] on [[Pantora]], which featured a [[Video Store (Pantora)|similar series of billboards]], but with a different motif. The stylized multicolored motif featured on the Pantoran billboards, resembling a kneeling figure,<ref name="Cornered" /> was also featured on [[Unidentified beverage|an alcoholic beverage]] served on Coruscant.<ref name="Peace">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref>

One video store was known as [[Pawp]] and was present on both Coruscant<ref name="Sabotage">{{TCW|Sabotage (episode)}}</ref> and Pantora,<ref name="Cornered" /> where a [[Pawp (advertisement)|third set of billboards]] was used to advertise the business.<ref name="Sabotage" />

==Behind the scenes==
The video store billboards on [[Pantora]] in the ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'' episode "[[Cornered]]" are not legible in the episode; however, the font and the text at the top<ref name="Cornered" /> has the same design as the one seen on billboards in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'',<ref name="DoM" /> and if you compare them, you can see that it is the same text.<ref name="Cornered" />
